claire: Draft async Rust snippet (keeps example minimal):
```rust
use redwood_rs::Client;
use std::time::Duration;
use tokio::time::sleep;

async fn gen_with_backoff(client: &Client, prompt: &str) -> anyhow::Result<String> {
    let mut attempt = 0u32;
    loop {
        match client.generate(prompt, 64).await {
            Ok(r) => return Ok(r.text),
            Err(e) => {
                if e.status == 429 && attempt < 4 {
                    let backoff = 2u64.pow(attempt) + rand::random::<u64>() % 500;
                    sleep(Duration::from_millis(backoff * 1000)).await;
                    attempt += 1;
                    continue;
                }
                return Err(e.into());
            }
        }
    }
}
```

claire: I'll add a tiny comment above the snippet: `// explicit 429 handling surfaces throttle signals; avoid SDK implicit retries in doc examples`

claire: Also adding a one-line "Context trimming" callout: "Trim long system prompts and repetitive history; prefer prefix/KV-cache retention tuning over unbounded context to avoid context-saturation 429s." Will link to /guides/context-limits.

