```yaml
fallback_policy:
  order:
    - regional_variant
    - edge_cached_variant
    - dedicated_pool
    - hosted_fallback
  max_attempts: 2
  notes: "prefer regional/edge cached variants for latency-sensitive workloads"
```

samir: Nice. Can we also surface an observability bulleted tip — what signals to watch to decide between backoff vs capacity changes? e.g., "burst 429s + stable p95 => backoff/regional; sustained 429s + rising p99 & queue depth => capacity/batching/KV-prefix retention". Keep it short.

claire: Will add that as a 1-line under "How to tell the difference." Also will split the Rust snippet into an include fragment after merge so the snippet linter can reuse it.

